.TH elf_section_index 3 "ELF Library Functions" "QuickJS" "ELF Library Functions"

.SH NAME
elf_section_index \- Retrieve the index of a section by its type

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/elf.h>
.B #include <lib/range.h>
.B int elf_section_index(void* elf, uint32_t sh_type);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The .B elf_section_index function retrieves the index of a section by its type.

The function takes two parameters:
.I elf
A pointer to the ELF file structure.
.I sh_type
The type of the section to find.

The function returns the index of the section if it is found. If the section is not found, the function returns -1.

.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the .B elf_section_index function:

.I
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/elf.h>
#include <lib/range.h>

int main() {
  // Assume elf is a valid pointer to an ELF file structure
  uint32_t sh_type = SHT_PROGBITS; // Example section type
  int index = elf_section_index(elf, sh_type);

  if (index != -1) {
    printf("Section index: %d\n", index);
  } else {
    printf("Section not found.\n");
  }

  return 0;
}
.!
